- **Per-instance prose variation** for repeated keys (bandits fires 2x word-for
-word in
  2/480 crossings). Vary prose/options by instance index in `SIGNATURE_CHOICES`
.
```

## Acceptance criteria

1. `git diff` (tracked files) touches ONLY: `web/src/utils/encounters.ts`,
   `web/src/utils/passage.ts`, `scripts/sim/passage-run.test.ts`, `ai/IDEAS.md`
.
   Nothing else. (`output/` is gitignored — the regenerated `output/sim/passage
-report.md`
   does NOT count and will not appear in `git diff`.)
2. `cd web && npx tsc -b` (or the repo's typecheck script) is clean.
3. Full test suite passes (`cd web && npm test -- --run`). The rewritten first
   regression test passes; no other test regresses. Report the pass/fail count.
   EXCEPTION: the second known-finding test ("Kheshkai → Qollari ... dies/abort
s with
   zero signature choices") — if it now fails because a promoted beat fires bef
ore
   death, do NOT edit it; report the failure to Opus and continue (Opus adjudic
ates,
   so this single failure does not block your handoff).
4. `cd web && npm run sim:passage` (FULL grid, no `--limit` — the sim is determ
inistic,
   so this guarantees the biome-gated `sabkha-sinkhole` appears) exits 0 and re
writes
   `output/sim/passage-report.md`. In that report, ALL of `dry-wadi`, `customs-
raid`,
   `plague-quarantine`, `sabkha-sinkhole` appear as keys in the per-signature-k
ey
   tables (proof they are wired as signatures). Paste the per-key table rows + 
the
   differentiation + outcome-impact rows for the 4 new keys into your handoff.
5. `cd web && npm run sim:passage-play -- --from kheshkai --to irrah --season w
inter`
   exits 0 and prints a journal. Paste the journal (or the portion showing any 
of the
   new choices, with their prompt + the chosen branch prose).
6. Report (do not fix): which of the 4 new keys show differentiation under STAN
DARD
   supply (water or rations range > 0.5, OR outcome-impact > 0), and which read
inert
   (expected for customs-raid "Give up the scribe").

